-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - the shared NOUNS.
--
-- Covers no section as a rule. It declares the things the whole Code talks
-- about, in the words a witness would use: persons (s 10, s 11), the particulars
-- of a charge (Criminal Procedure Code 2010 s 124), property (s 22), documents,
-- electronic records and instruments (ss 29-31A), offices (s 21), places, and
-- the fault words (ss 26C-26F) as a vocabulary.
--
-- DECLARE and nothing else. The membership test: could a witness of ordinary
-- competence testify to it? If answering needs the Code, it is a rule, and it
-- lives in pc-general.l4 (Chapter 2) or in the module that owns its section.
--
-- Every other module IMPORTs this one and never redeclares what it declares.
-- A noun a group needs that is missing here is declared in that group's own
-- module and proposed for this one in the group's report.
--
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO "Current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026" (inputs/PC1871.txt).

§ `Penal Code 1871 - shared nouns`

§§ `Persons`

-- A charge speaks of a person in the third person ("by deceiving HER to
-- believe"). s 8: "he" and its derivatives are used of any person, male or
-- female - so the Code's own text needs no pronoun, but the charge does.
DECLARE Pronoun IS ONE OF
    he
    she
    they

-- s 10: "man" denotes a male human being of any age; "woman" a female human
-- being of any age. The sex is the witness's fact; the word is s 10's rule.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 10
DECLARE Sex IS ONE OF
    male
    female

-- s 11: "person" includes any company or association or body of persons,
-- whether incorporated or not.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 11
DECLARE `Kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `a human being`
    `a company`
    `an association`
    `a body of persons`

-- The person as a charge names them: "one Wong Fei Hsia, the cashier of Seiyu
-- Departmental Store". Only what a recital needs. Age and sex, where a section
-- turns on them, are fields of that offence's facts record (see notes/PLAN.md
-- §4), because they are elements there and particulars here.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 11; Criminal Procedure Code 2010 s 124(1) - "the person (if any) against whom ... it was committed"
DECLARE Person HAS
    name             IS A STRING          @desc The person's name, as it is to appear in the charge - for example "Wong Fei Hsia"
    `described as`   IS A STRING          @desc How the charge describes the person after the name - for example "the cashier of Seiyu Departmental Store"; leave blank if not needed
    pronoun          IS A Pronoun         @desc The pronoun the charge uses for the person
    kind             IS A `Kind of person` @desc Whether the person is a human being, a company, an association or a body of persons (s 11)

§§ `The particulars of a charge`

-- Criminal Procedure Code 2010 s 124(1): "such particulars as to the time and
-- place of the alleged offence and the person (if any) against whom or the
-- thing (if any) in respect of which it was committed". Identical, field for
-- field, to the reference row's `Particulars`, which the charge generator
-- fills.
@ref Criminal Procedure Code 2010 s 124(1) - time, place and person; Penal Code 1871 s 34 for the joint-charge rider
DECLARE Particulars HAS
    accused            IS A STRING  @desc The accused person's full name, as it is to appear in the charge
    date               IS A STRING  @desc The date of the offence, as it is to read after "on or about" - for example "the 24th day of April 2000"
    time               IS A STRING  @desc The time of day, as it is to read after "at about" - for example "8.10 pm"; leave blank if not known
    place              IS A STRING  @desc Where the offence was committed, as it is to read after "at" - "Singapore" is added for you
    `co-accused`       IS A STRING  @desc Anyone charged jointly with the accused, as they are to be named in the charge; leave blank if none
    `common intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done in furtherance of a common intention shared with the co-accused, so that section 34 is read with the charge?

§§ `Places`

-- s 2 (within Singapore), s 3 (beyond Singapore), s 4B (partly in, partly
-- out). Where a place is, is a witness's fact.
@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 2, 3, 4, 4A, 4B
DECLARE Place HAS
    description        IS A STRING  @desc The place, as it is to read in a charge
    `within Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place within Singapore?

§§ `Property - s 22`

-- The atoms of s 22's four definitions. Whether a thing IS "movable property"
-- is s 22's rule (pc-general.l4); whether it is land, or is fastened to the
-- earth, is a witness's fact.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 22 - the operative atoms of "immovable property", "movable property", "property" and "virtual currency"
DECLARE `Property` HAS
    description        IS A STRING  @desc The property, as it is to read in a charge - for example "one Nokia handphone"
    `is land`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it land?
    `is a benefit to arise out of land`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a benefit to arise out of land?
    `is a thing attached to the earth`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a thing attached to the earth?
    `is permanently fastened to anything attached to the earth`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it permanently fastened to anything attached to the earth?
    `is money`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it money?
    `is a thing in action`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a thing in action (a right enforceable only by legal action, such as a debt or a bank balance)?
    `is other intangible or incorporeal property`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it some other intangible or incorporeal property?
    `is a digital representation of value in money or money's worth`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a digital representation of value in money or money's worth?
    `can be digitally traded`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can it be digitally traded?
    `functions as a medium of exchange, a unit of account or store of value`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it function as a medium of exchange, a unit of account or a store of value (whether or not it is legal tender anywhere)?

§§ `Documents, electronic records and instruments - ss 29-31A`

-- The atoms of ss 29, 29A, 29B, 30, 31 and 31A's "instrument". One record,
-- because the Code's words overlap: a valuable security is a document or an
-- electronic record (s 30); an instrument includes any document (s 31A).
@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 29, 29A, 29B, 30, 31, 31A - the operative atoms
DECLARE Document HAS
    description        IS A STRING  @desc The document, as it is to read in a charge - for example "a cheque for $5,000 drawn on DBS Bank"
    -- s 29 and s 29A
    `is a document in writing`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a document in writing - words, figures, drawings or symbols represented or reproduced in a visible form (s 29A)?
    `is a map, plan, graph or drawing`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a map, plan, graph or drawing? (s 29(a))
    `is a photograph`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a photograph? (s 29(b))
    `is a label, marking or other writing identifying or describing a thing it forms part of or is attached to`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a label, marking or other writing which identifies or describes anything it forms part of or is attached to? (s 29(c))
    `is a device embodying sounds or other data capable of being reproduced`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a disc, tape, soundtrack or other device in which sounds or other data (not visual images) are embodied so as to be capable of being reproduced? (s 29(d))
    `is a device embodying visual images capable of being reproduced`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a film, microfilm, negative, tape, disc or other device in which visual images are embodied so as to be capable of being reproduced? (s 29(e))
    `is material bearing marks having a meaning for persons qualified to interpret them`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paper or other material bearing marks, impressions, figures, letters, symbols or perforations having a meaning for persons qualified to interpret them? (s 29(f))
    -- s 29B
    `is an electronic record`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an electronic record within the meaning of the Electronic Transactions Act 2010 (s 29B)? That Act is not encoded here.
    -- s 30
    `is or purports to be a document whereby a legal right is created, extended, transferred, restricted, extinguished or released`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it (or does it purport to) create, extend, transfer, restrict, extinguish or release a legal right? (s 30(1))
    `is or purports to be a document whereby a person acknowledges legal liability or that he has not a certain legal right`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a person by it (or purportedly by it) acknowledge that he lies under legal liability, or has not a certain legal right? (s 30(1))
    `is a card which has money or money's worth or other financial rights attached`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a credit card, charge card, stored value card, ATM card or other card with money, money's worth or other financial rights attached? (s 30(2))
    -- s 31
    `is testamentary`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it testamentary - does it dispose of property on death? (s 31)
    -- s 31A "instrument"
    `is a postage stamp or revenue stamp`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a postage stamp or a revenue stamp? (s 31A)
    `is a seal or die` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a seal, or a die - a plate, type, tool, chop or implement, a part of one, or a stamp or impression of one? (s 31A)
    `is a device on or in which information is recorded or stored`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a disc, card, tape, microchip, soundtrack or other device on or in which information is recorded or stored by mechanical, electronic, optical or other means? (s 31A)

§§ `Offices - s 21`

-- The descriptions in s 21(1)(a)-(j), as facts about the office a person holds
-- and the duties it carries. Whether the holder IS a "public servant" is
-- s 21's rule (pc-general.l4).
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 21 - the operative atoms of subsection (1)(a)-(j) and subsection (2); Explanations 1 and 2 are why none of them asks how the person was appointed
DECLARE Office HAS
    description        IS A STRING  @desc The office or employment, as it is to read in a charge - for example "a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division"
    `officer in the Singapore Armed Forces`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) Is the person an officer in the Singapore Armed Forces?
    `is a judge`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Is the person a judge (s 19)?
    `officer of a court of justice with a judicial duty`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) Is the person an officer of a court of justice whose duty as such is to investigate or report on law or fact, make, authenticate or keep a document, take charge of or dispose of property, execute judicial process, administer an oath, interpret, preserve order in court, or conduct mediation or other ADR under written law - or specially authorised by a court to do any of these?
    `assessor assisting a court of justice or public servant`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc (d) Is the person an assessor assisting a court of justice or a public servant?
    `arbitrator or referee of a court or competent public authority`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc (e) Is the person an arbitrator or other person to whom a cause or matter has been referred for decision or report by a court of justice or other competent public authority?
    `holds an office empowering him to place or keep a person in confinement`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc (f) Does the person hold an office by virtue of which he is empowered to place or keep any person in confinement?
    `officer of the Government or of a statutory body for a public function`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc (g) Is the person an officer of the Government, or an officer or employee of a body corporate established by a public Act for the purposes of a public function?
    `duty of maintaining law and order`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc (g)(i) Is it the person's duty to maintain law and order?
    `duty of preserving the public peace`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc (g)(ii) ... to preserve the public peace?
    `duty of preventing and detecting offences`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc (g)(iii) ... to prevent and detect offences?
    `duty of apprehending offenders or bringing them to justice`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc (g)(iv) ... to apprehend offenders or otherwise bring offenders to justice?
    `duty of executing legal processes`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc (g)(v) ... to execute summonses, subpoenas, orders to attend court, warrants, commitments and other legal processes issued by a court or a Justice of the Peace?
    `duty of maintaining order in the premises of the courts`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc (g)(vi) ... to maintain order in the premises of the courts of justice?
    `duty of escorting and guarding prisoners and accused persons in remand`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc (g)(vii) ... to escort and guard prisoners and accused persons in remand?
    `duty of protecting public health or safety or preventing public inconvenience`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc (g)(viii) ... to protect public health or safety or prevent public inconvenience?
    `officer with a duty touching the property or pecuniary interests of Government, or in the service or pay of Government, or remunerated for a public duty`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc (h) Is the person an officer whose duty is to take, receive, keep or expend property on behalf of Government, make a survey, assessment or contract for it, execute revenue process, investigate or report on or keep documents about its pecuniary interests, or prevent infraction of laws protecting them - or an officer in the service or pay of Government, or remunerated by fees or commission for a public duty?
    `member of the Public Service, Judicial Service or Legal Service Commission`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc (i) Is the person a member of the Public Service Commission, the Judicial Service Commission or the Legal Service Commission?
    `employed to carry out a duty in paragraph (g)(i) to (vii) on behalf of the Government or a statutory body`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc (j) Is the person (not within paragraph (g)) employed to carry out any of the duties in (g)(i)-(vii) on behalf of the Government or a body corporate established by a public Act for a public function?
    `performing such duties at the time`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc (j) Was that person performing such duties at the time in question?
    `a judge as defined in the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016`
                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a judge as defined in the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016? (s 21(2): not a public servant for ss 175, 178, 179, 180 and 228)

§§ `The fault words - ss 22A, 26C-26F`

-- The Code's own names for the states of mind an offence may require. This is
-- a vocabulary, not a verdict: which one a particular act was done with is
-- decided by ss 26C-26F (pc-general.l4) over their own atoms, and s 26D(3),
-- s 26E(3) and s 26F(2) say which ones satisfy which.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 22A(1) ("intention, wilfulness, knowledge, rashness and negligence"), ss 26C-26F, s 26D(3) ("wilful blindness")
DECLARE `Fault word` IS ONE OF
    intentionally
    knowingly
    `with wilful blindness`
    rashly
    negligently
